I checked all five model ids against the vendors' own pages, and none of them is a model you can actually call. All five are gone from the provider lists and from /model Tab completion. Typing one now prints the "Unknown model" warning instead of being let through silently. None of them was a provider's default, so no default changed. Committed as 607d0dbc ("Part of #1147"); fmt, clippy with -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

| id | provider | verdict | source |
|---|---|---|---|
| o4-mini-high | openai | not an API id | its OpenAI docs page is a 404, and the all-models page lists only o4-mini and o4-mini-deep-research |
| gpt-5.5-mini | openai | not real | docs page is a 404; only gpt-5.5 and gpt-5.5-pro exist |
| mixtral-8x7b-32768 | groq | retired | Groq's deprecations page: "March 20, 2025: Mixtral 8x7B" |
| grok-2 | xai | retired | missing from xAI's models page. I couldn't find xAI's own retirement notice; the "retired by xAI" error text comes from reports on litellm#38179 and #38510 |
| MiniMax-M1-40k | minimax | not an API id | MiniMax's text API names MiniMax-M1, never -40k |

